.TH AUDIO-TOOLS 1 "May 2026" "audio-tools v3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
audio-tools \- convert, clean, normalize, dedup, and organize audio files from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B audio-tools
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]
.br
.B audio-tools \fI\,COMMAND\/\fR [\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] [\fI\,FILE\/\fR|\fI\,DIR\/\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B audio-tools
batch-processes audio files using ffmpeg.
It converts WAV, OGG, FLAC, AAC, WMA, and M4A between formats,
normalizes loudness (EBU R128), trims/splits silence, concatenates
files, removes short/long recordings, sanitizes filenames, renames
with patterns, deduplicates by SHA256, consolidates scattered audio
into one directory, and searches by filename keyword.
.PP
When run without arguments,
.B audio-tools
starts an interactive menu that guides you through each action: it
prompts for source directories, output paths, thresholds, and
confirmation before destructive operations.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "Conversion & Processing"
.TP
.B convert
Convert WAV/OGG/FLAC/AAC/WMA/M4A to MP3 (default), OGG, AAC, or FLAC
with configurable bitrate. Output directory: converted_mp3
(configurable via AUDIO_TOOLS_CONVERTED_DIR).
Options: \fB--format\fR, \fB--bitrate\fR, \fB--output\fR.
.TP
.B normalize
Normalize loudness using EBU R128 standard (\-16 LUFS target).
Output goes to a \fBprocessed\fR subdirectory.
.TP
.B trim-silence
Remove leading and trailing silence from audio files.
Output goes to a \fBprocessed\fR subdirectory.
.TP
.B split-silence \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Split a single audio file at silence points into multiple segments.
Output goes to a \fB{filename}_split\fR directory.
.TP
.B concat
Concatenate multiple audio files in a directory into one file.
Files are joined in alphabetical order. Output: concatenated.mp3.
.SS "Cleanup & Organize"
.TP
.B clean
Replace spaces with underscores and strip special characters from
filenames in the target directory. Operates in place.
.TP
.B rename
Batch rename audio files using pattern tokens:
\fB{n}\fR (sequential number), \fB{orig}\fR (original name),
\fB{date}\fR (YYYYMMDD_XXXXXX with random suffix), \fB{ext}\fR (file extension).
The extension auto-preserves if not included in the pattern.
Requires: \fB--pattern\fR.
.TP
.B scan
Recursively find all audio files in subdirectories and copy them into a
single flat directory. Duplicate names are suffixed with _1, _2, etc.
Output directory: ALL_AUDIOS (configurable via AUDIO_TOOLS_SCAN_DIR).
.TP
.B remove \fI\,short\|long\/\fR
Find audio files shorter/longer than \fB--threshold\fR seconds and
move them to the system trash. Requires: \fB--threshold\fR.
Aliases: \fBremove-short\fR, \fBremove-long\fR.
.TP
.B dedup
Find exact duplicates by SHA256 hash and move all but the first file
to the system trash.
.SS "Inspect & Search"
.TP
.B find-dupes
Find exact duplicates by SHA256 hash and display groups.
No files are deleted.
.TP
.B list
List audio files with metadata. Supports output formats:
\fBtable\fR (default), \fBsimple\fR, \fBtree\fR.
.TP
.B stats
Show aggregate directory statistics: file count, total duration,
total size, breakdown by format. Supports \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B info
Display metadata for a single audio file (bitrate, channels,
sample rate, duration, format). Supports \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.B search
Find audio files whose filename contains \fB--query\fR and either
delete or extract them. Extract copies to a \fB{query}_extracted\fR
subdirectory. Requires: \fB--query\fR and \fB--operation\fR
(delete or extract).
.SS "Shell & Config"
.TP
.B config
Manage configuration. Subcommands:
\fBlist\fR, \fBget\fR \fI\,KEY\/\fR, \fBset\fR \fI\,KEY VALUE\/\fR,
\fBreset\fR, \fBedit\fR (opens $EDITOR), \fBpath\fR (show file path).
.TP
.B completion
Generate shell completion script for \fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR, or \fBfish\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-directory \fI\,PATH\/\fR
Target directory (default: current directory).
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Skip all confirmation prompts (use with caution).
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-threshold \fI\,SECONDS\/\fR
Duration threshold for
.B remove
(subcommands short/long).
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-query \fI\,STRING\/\fR
Filename keyword for
.BR search .
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-operation \fI\,OP\/\fR
Operation for
.BR search :
.B delete
or
.BR extract .
.TP
.B \-\-format \fI\,FMT\/\fR
Output format for
.BR convert
(mp3/ogg/aac/flac) or
.BR list
(table/simple/tree).
.TP
.B \-\-bitrate \fI\,RATE\/\fR
Audio bitrate for convert (default: 320k).
.TP
.B \-\-pattern \fI\,PAT\/\fR
Rename pattern for
.BR rename :
tokens {n}, {orig}, {date}, {ext}.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output results in JSON format.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Simulate operation without modifying files.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Show detailed step-by-step output.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress information and warning output.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI colored output.
.TP
.B \-C, \-\-config \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Use custom config file path.
.TP
.B \-\-files-from \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Read file paths from a file (one per line).
.TP
.B \-\-max-depth \fI\,N\/\fR
Maximum recursion depth (default: unlimited).
.TP
.B \-\-progress
Show compact progress bar (default).
.TP
.B \-\-no-progress
Show detailed per-file logs instead.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AUDIO_TOOLS_CONVERTED_DIR
Output subdirectory name for
.BR convert .
Default: converted_mp3.
.TP
.B AUDIO_TOOLS_SCAN_DIR
Output subdirectory name for
.BR scan .
Default: ALL_AUDIOS.
.TP
.B AUDIO_TOOLS_FORMAT
Default output format for convert (default: mp3).
.TP
.B AUDIO_TOOLS_BITRATE
Default audio bitrate for convert (default: 320k).
.TP
.B AUDIO_TOOLS_CONFIG
Path to the configuration file.
Default: ~/.config/audio-tools/config.sh.
.TP
.B AUDIO_TOOLS_FORCE
Skip all confirmation prompts when set to
.BR yes .
.TP
.B AUDIO_TOOLS_QUIET
Suppress output when set to
.BR yes .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI color in output when set (any non-empty value).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/audio-tools/config.sh
Optional configuration file. Plain Bash syntax, sourced at startup.
Can set any of the environment variables listed above.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
64
Usage error (invalid flag, missing required argument).
.TP
65
Data error (bad file).
.TP
69
Service unavailable (ffmpeg or ffprobe not installed).
.TP
74
I/O error (file read or write failure).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Convert all audio in the current directory
.RS
.nf
audio-tools convert
.fi
.RE
.TP
Convert to FLAC with custom bitrate
.RS
.nf
audio-tools convert --format flac --bitrate 192k ./samples
.fi
.RE
.TP
Remove files shorter than 2 seconds (non-interactive)
.RS
.nf
audio-tools remove short --threshold 2 --directory ./samples
.fi
.RE
.TP
Force-delete files longer than 30 seconds
.RS
.nf
audio-tools remove long --threshold 30 --force
.fi
.RE
.TP
Search for kick drum samples and extract them
.RS
.nf
audio-tools search --query kick --operation extract ./samples
.fi
.RE
.TP
Normalize loudness (dry run first)
.RS
.nf
audio-tools normalize --dry-run ./library
.fi
.RE
.TP
Rename files with sequential pattern
.RS
.nf
audio-tools rename --pattern 'track_{n}_{orig}' ./tracks
.fi
.RE
.TP
Find duplicates
.RS
.nf
audio-tools find-dupes ./audio
.fi
.RE
.TP
Remove duplicates
.RS
.nf
audio-tools dedup ./audio --force
.fi
.RE
.TP
Show directory statistics
.RS
.nf
audio-tools stats ./library --json
.fi
.RE
.TP
Launch the interactive menu
.RS
.nf
audio-tools
.fi
.RE
